  "id": "Sweeping_Credential_Harvesting_Heist_Compromises_30K_Fortinet_Devices_txt_8",
  "content": "\"The most striking thing about the FortiBleed breach is what's missing from it,\" Waseem Ahmed, head of engineering at Secure.com, tells Dark Reading. \"There's no zero-day, no exploit, no actual 'bleed.' Despite the name, this isn't a vulnerability but a pile of credentials leaked in earlier Fortinet breaches, fired back at organizations that never bothered to change them.\"",
